# SINGLE-OWNER SUB-PLACE NEG — CAPTURE axis: a DROPPABLE capture (`String`),
# where the int-capturing cells hold a non-droppable one. The env block's drop
# strategy differs between the two, so a fix that happened to work only for a
# POD env would leave this cell live. Named as its own row rather than assumed
# equivalent (an axis sampled at one value is an anecdote, not a net).
#
# Omitted cell: bare INDEX places are deferred behind the callee-borrow ruling
# (todo/t1225).
#
# CELL: type=Callable · place=field of a local · position=bind · capture=STRING.
# RED at 7bf11017e: `gg check` ACCEPTED (rc 0).
# ggdef: ABSTAIN (todo/t1227).

struct Holder:
    Callable[String()] f

Callable[String()] mk(String s):
    return (): s + "!"

void main():
    Holder h = Holder(mk("hi"))
    Callable[String()] g = h.f
    print(g())
